 {'id': 'continual_arc_task_ae6991c2_extend_exposed_diagonal_pairs', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'Continual-ARC task-ae6991c2: extend exposed diagonal marker pairs', 'content': "Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-ae6991c2, confirmed across prior demonstrations and this correctly solved 23×29 recurrence. On a uniform-background grid, identify matching-color diagonal sequences with at least two cells, then extend their exposed ends along that diagonal through background cells. A diagonal step changes row and column by one; extend until the grid border or stop immediately before any non-background obstacle. Preserve all original cells, grid dimensions, and background. Do not extend a singleton merely because it is collinear with another color's diagonal run. Horizontal or vertical pairs alone are not extended merely because they are aligned. In this recurrence, the 6 pair at (9,2),(10,3) extended up-left to (7,0); the 2 pair at (9,5),(10,4) extended up-right to (0,14); the 0 pair at (11,3),(12,2) extended down-left to (14,0); singleton 8 at (11,4) stayed unchanged. This confirms distinct-color sequences on one diagonal extend independently, and singleton 8 must not be extended. Two earlier submissions failed: the first extended 6/8 but omitted 2/0; the second added 2/0 but also extended singleton 8. Implementation caution: derive cells using the appropriate constant r+c or r-c invariant, check each coordinate carefully, and validate every output row length; an off-by-one placement caused a previous submission failure.\nAdditional recurrence evidence (task grid 18×22): color 9 pair (8,3),(9,4) extends up-left to (5,0); the down-right extension stops at existing color 2 at (10,5). On the opposite diagonal, color 6 pair (8,6),(9,5) extends up-right to (0,14), while color 7 pair (10,4),(11,3) extends down-left to (14,0); color 2 and original pixels are preserved. A separate 6×21 demonstration contained an isolated small color-4 diagonal-looking motif and was unchanged, so apply this to the established marker-track pattern rather than extending any arbitrary diagonal-looking decorative object. The prior 23×29 recurrence and this recurrence both confirm independent extension of different-color runs on a shared diagonal, stopping before non-background blockers.\n", 'path': 'continual_arc', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {'scope': 'global', 'latest_evidence': 'correct test task-ae6991c2 recurrence with 2 demos'}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-09-29T13:26:40.770576+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-09-29T16:28:05.923045+00:00', 'version': 5}
